<title>FRANCE: Tugboat strike in southern France delaying crude.</title>
<headline>Tugboat strike in southern France delaying crude.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>A sporadic tugboat strike in the southern French port of Fos has hardened in the past week, preventing tankers from unloading their shipments of crude oil, port officials said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>They said a strike that began over a month ago in the Mediterranean port city near Marseille had been suspended on and off during its first three weeks while sporadic negotiations took place.</p>
<p>However, in the past week, efforts at negotiation had failed and the strikers have now stopped working altogether, they said.</p>
<p>The strike was preventing crude oil shipments from reaching area refineries including Shell's Berre refinery and British Petroleum's Lavera facility.</p>
<p>The strike at Fos was not affecting operations at the port of Marseille, officials there said.</p>
</text>
